{
 "thread": "CmUxGuk0-28",
 "subject": "Problem with installing pool package on shinyapps.io",
 "messages_listed": 3,
 "last_activity": "2017-05-17T22:44:21Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "uIL43jytBAAJ",
   "from": "Dennis Andersen",
   "author": "f3fefe9460a71c74",
   "date": "2017-05-17T02:03:30Z",
   "subject": "Problem with installing pool package on shinyapps.io",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">When deploying app to <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792360989924000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2OjswiAEZTmKMUiBm8bWN0\">shinyapps.io</a> that has a dependency on the pool package the following error is received:<br><pre style=\"font-family:Consolas!important;font-size:10pt!important;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;box-sizing:border-box;width:1018px;padding:6px;color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"> Building R package: pool (0.1.0)\r\n/mnt/packages/build /mnt\r\nWarning in untar2(tarfile, files, list, exdir, restore_times) :\r\n  skipping pax global extended headers\r\n* installing to library �/usr/local/lib/R/site-library�\r\n* installing *source* package �p</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">ool� ...\r\n** R\r\n** preparing package for lazy loading\r\nError in conformMethod(signature, mnames, fnames, f, fdef, definition) : \r\n  in method for �sqlInterpolate� with signature �conn=&quot;Pool&quot;�: formal arguments (conn = &quot;Pool&quot;, sql = &quot;Pool&quot;, ... = &quot;Pool&quot;, .dots = &quot;Pool&quot;) omitted in the method definition cannot be in the signature\r\nError : unable to load R code in package �pool�\r\nERROR: lazy loading failed for package �pool�<br><br><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\">I am running the 3.4.0patched version of R locally and Version 1.0.143 of RStudio.<br><br><br>Any ideas on how to get around this?<br><br>Thanks,<br>Dennis</font></span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Segoe UI&#39;;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(243,244,244)\"></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Segoe UI&#39;;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(243,244,244);display:inline!important;float:none\"><span></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Segoe UI&#39;;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(243,244,244)\"></span></font></span></pre></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "mKyX6AjUBAAJ",
   "from": "Joshua Spiewak",
   "author": "299a5089d6c6c523",
   "date": "2017-05-17T13:54:28Z",
   "subject": "Re: Problem with installing pool package on shinyapps.io",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I reached out to my co-worker who developed the pool package, and she suggested updating your version of DBI. Her full response was:<div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\">Hi Josh,</span></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\"><br></div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\">I actually know exactly what&#39;s causing this and it can be solved by upgrading to the latest DBI version on CRAN (or latest development version will do too). Basically, DBI &gt; 0.6 breaks back compatibility because they change a method signature (the error above). As soon as that was released on CRAN, I also updated pool to be compatible with the current DBI.</div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\"><br></div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\">So, it seems that that user has an old version of DBI and the current version of pool.</div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\"><br></div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\">That error can reproed with these commands:</div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\"><br></div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"># With DBI &lt; 0.6, trying to install pool results in an error</font></blockquote></div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">devtools::install_github(&quot;cran/DBI@882c3921ee58d1fa97298697bf2a50161a8e401a&quot;)</font></blockquote></div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">devtools::install_github(&quot;rstudio/pool&quot;)</font></blockquote></div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\"><div><br></div></div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\">By upgrading DBI, the problem goes away:</div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\"><br></div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"># With current DBI, all is good</font></blockquote></div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">install.packages(&quot;DBI&quot;)</font></blockquote></div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">devtools::install_github(&quot;rstudio/pool&quot;)</font></blockquote></div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\"><br></div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\">Let me know if anything else comes up... Thanks!</div></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:sans-serif\">Barbara</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Tuesday, May 16, 2017 at 10:03:30 PM UTC-4, Dennis Andersen wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">When deploying app to <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792360989927000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3wLfesluAKNrRXyHrwnfwK\">shinyapps.io</a> that has a dependency on the pool package the following error is received:<br><pre style=\"font-family:Consolas!important;font-size:10pt!important;font-style:inherit!important;font-variant:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;width:1018px;padding:6px;color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"> Building R package: pool (0.1.0)\r\n/mnt/packages/build /mnt\r\nWarning in untar2(tarfile, files, list, exdir, restore_times) :\r\n  skipping pax global extended headers\r\n* installing to library �/usr/local/lib/R/site-library�\r\n* installing *source* package �p</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">ool� ...\r\n** R\r\n** preparing package for lazy loading\r\nError in conformMethod(signature, mnames, fnames, f, fdef, definition) : \r\n  in method for �sqlInterpolate� with signature �conn=&quot;Pool&quot;�: formal arguments (conn = &quot;Pool&quot;, sql = &quot;Pool&quot;, ... = &quot;Pool&quot;, .dots = &quot;Pool&quot;) omitted in the method definition cannot be in the signature\r\nError : unable to load R code in package �pool�\r\nERROR: lazy loading failed for package �pool�<br><br><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\">I am running the 3.4.0patched version of R locally and Version 1.0.143 of RStudio.<br><br><br>Any ideas on how to get around this?<br><br>Thanks,<br>Dennis</font></span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Segoe UI&#39;;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(243,244,244)\"></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Segoe UI&#39;;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(243,244,244);display:inline!important;float:none\"><span></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Segoe UI&#39;;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(243,244,244)\"></span></font></span></pre></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
